
Dictonaries are used to store data values in the foem of (key:value) pairs.
It is ordered , changeable and do not allow duplicate value.((changeble:value can be changed on index)).
Values can be same but keys cant be same.
Key cant be null but value can be null.
Dictionary in python is same as json of javascript and also hashmap in java.

Syntax:

1. Basic syntax

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","dob":"12-2-2002"}
print(mydict)

2.  Here the city value wuill be updated from indore to ujjain (it will take ujjain for the city key)

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","city":, "ujjain"}
print(mydict)

3. Key storing multiple value for colour

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
print(mydict)

4. Creating dictioanry using constructor((dict))

m=dict(name="kusj", city="indore")
print(m)

5. Accesing the element from the key and get method(( here we have to give key name for the both to get teh value))

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
print(mydict["name"])
print(mydict.get("city"))

6. keys method and value method to get list of keys and value present in the dictionary

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
x=mydict.keys()
print(x)
y=mydict.values()
print(y)

7. items method (it will return each item in a dictionary as tuples in a list)


mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
x=mydict.items()
print(x)


8. in & not in  ( it will work on keys not in values)(true if present otherwise fale)

mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
x="name" in mydict
print(x)


mydict={"name":"Kush", "city": "indore","course":"btech","colour":["r", "g"]}
x="age" not in mydict
print(x)
